{"title":"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As shown in the figure, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> be a regular hexagon of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9456e0361813641f4ce80980839e9038fe8f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are drawn centered at vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, forming a curved triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. What is the perimeter of this curved triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fadaa7a7afecd74e4f58b985fa43d06a57e27b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\sqrt{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{3}\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"445\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Screenshot_2026-08-11_201600.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8a/Screenshot_2026-08-11_201600.png/340px-Screenshot_2026-08-11_201600.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"340\" height=\"317\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/8/8a/Screenshot_2026-08-11_201600.png/510px-Screenshot_2026-08-11_201600.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8a/Screenshot_2026-08-11_201600.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the perimeter of the curved triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, we need to find the total length of the three congruent circular arcs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9456e0361813641f4ce80980839e9038fe8f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let us consider arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, which is centered at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. In a regular hexagon with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the distance between two alternating vertices (such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) is the long diagonal of a rhombus formed by two adjacent equilateral triangles, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the radius of the circle containing arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/f/37fb67a691a78158ab515f5f4a5c488b8283bd88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />. Next, we determine the central angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3eddba1b3d73e20a58d18dd47b4615d258155333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEC$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> subtended by this arc. The interior angle of a regular hexagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fd424e953ac76b50bf6103875acc049d21d3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. Looking at the isosceles triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f417bb6ca3203bac2147a52b18e0c3de95444f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFA$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/a/7aa1285028ff4b669c297c1ad712708a93694c16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EDC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/8704124f3e01fa51db34935cdffff71509113c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FEA = \\angle DEC = \\frac{180^\\circ - 120^\\circ}{2} = 30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"309\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, the central angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dce0dcd6b5b5b5f67051a5f1eeb8f43b745622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEC = 120^\\circ - 30^\\circ - 30^\\circ = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"262\" height=\"16\" />. The length of a single arc with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> central angle is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644e29b19fb7ffe0323ae6ae1dfa08f918be6986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60^\\circ}{360^\\circ} = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"39\" /> of the circumference of a full circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, which evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02b6ef98a251c219c0513411c8291e996c933495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6} \\times 2\\pi\\sqrt{3} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"43\" />. Since the curved triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f348b5890100fa57eaa4a3c548badc83b75af585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is bounded by three symmetric arcs of equal length, the total perimeter is obtained by multiplying the length of one arc by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd283e6860e592d51bf488289501594bed8f318b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\pi = \\sqrt{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d98555a3915f31d21cea7aeb782df10cbab9f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{3}\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"83\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~Icoshahedron0288\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_8_Regional_Problems\" title=\"2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems\">2026 AMC 8 Regional Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034328\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 199/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6778/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37409:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034328 and revision id 291935. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}